{"nodes": [{"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_ldo3_report", "label": "Three-Disease Leave-One-Disease-Out Results", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Generated by ldo3_report.py from results/lodo artifacts: 3 held-out diseases x 5 seeds = 15 runs, country-macro headline, nothing averaged across datasets."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_negative_transfer_finding", "label": "Cross-Disease Transfer Is Negative (25 of 36 Cells)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With the disease genuinely held out and judged by the paired origin bootstrap: 25 cells significantly worse than the single-disease ceiling, 10 within noise, 1 better. The adapted arm is the optimistic bound because the held-out disease got its entire train fold to fit the adapter."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_horizon_gradient", "label": "Transfer Degrades Monotonically with Horizon", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At h3 the transfer arm is close to parity with a model trained on the disease itself; by h10 and h15 it is uniformly and substantially worse, reaching -38% and -51%. A frozen foreign trunk carries short-range structure for a few weeks ahead and then loses it."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_zero_shot_arm_failure", "label": "The Zero-Shot Arm Fails Everywhere", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The borrowed mean adapter is behind the ceiling in 36 of 36 attributable cells, 34 significantly, and ahead in none; averaging in-disease adapters produces nothing usable on an unseen disease."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_option_b_decision", "label": "Option B: The Disease Must Be Trained On Directly", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The trunk does not transfer across diseases well enough to carry a held-out disease, and Ebola will have 27 labelled support cells rather than a train fold, so few-shot Ebola cannot do better than these numbers and will very likely do worse."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_covid_omicron_exclusion", "label": "COVID Long Horizons Excluded, Not Counted as Losses", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The COVID test fold is a flat tail on the far side of the Omicron break while selection happens on the surge, so h10 and h15 measure a fold boundary rather than transfer. Applied symmetrically: the ceiling is degraded by the same break, so no positive COVID claim is made either."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_paired_origin_bootstrap", "label": "Paired Bootstrap Over Time Origins (B=10,000)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rebuilds both arms from the same resampled origins so shared origin noise cancels; covers RMSE and MAE only, because PCC is not additive over origins from the stored sufficient statistics."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_uq_block", "label": "Uncertainty Metrics Block", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WIS, CRPS, coverage of the central 50% and 90% intervals and mean width, computed from archived quantiles in count space over the same cells and node set as the point metrics."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_wis_crps_identity", "label": "WIS and CRPS Are the Same Number on a Symmetric 5-Level Grid", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Algebraically identical on this grid, so both columns are printed only because the Review Doc names both metrics and they must not be cited as independent evidence; they would separate only on an asymmetric or denser grid."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_zero_shot_no_quantiles_gap", "label": "Zero-Shot Arm Has No Archived Quantiles", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "run_ldo3_fold passes quant_out only for the adapted arm, so WIS, CRPS, coverage and PIT cannot be computed for zero-shot without re-running the fold."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_fold_confounding_caveat", "label": "Every Fold Varies Graph, Geography and Node Count", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three held-out diseases with one bundle for dengue, one for COVID and three for influenza is the whole cross-disease evidence base, so a negative here is not attributable to the disease change on its own; the graph-controlled COVID/influenza-US-states pair is the fold that isolates the disease."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_bootstrap_vs_seed_paired_disagreement", "label": "Where the Bootstrap Disagrees with the Seed-Paired Test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "They are two different quantities, not two measurements of one: section 2 averages per-node scores while the bootstrap pools cells before the square root, and on COVID the state-level counts span orders of magnitude. No positive COVID transfer claim is made because the arm producing positives does not survive the other test."}], "edges": [{"source": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_ldo3_report", "target": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_negative_transfer_finding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_ldo3_report", "target": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_horizon_gradient", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_ldo3_report", "target": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_zero_shot_arm_failure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_ldo3_report", "target": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_option_b_decision", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/LDO3_Results.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_ldo3_report", "target": "progress_outcomes_ldo3_results_covid_omicron_exclusion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file